3
00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.861
in black for her wedding.

4
00:00:06.861 --> 00:00:07.694
Yeah.

5
00:00:07.694 --> 00:00:09.150
And that I empathize with her

6
00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.504
because my daughter wanted a death-themed birthday party.

7
00:00:12.504 --> 00:00:13.337
Yeah.
And I was like,

8
00:00:13.337 --> 00:00:14.630
"I can't scare the other parents."

9
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.323
And then the invitation is that.

10
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.640
And... (chuckles)

11
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.530
She's my girl, okay?

12
00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:22.363
Wait.
(audience laughs)

13
00:00:22.363 --> 00:00:24.010
I had a birthday party like that, too.

14
00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:25.780
Okay, so tell me about this birthday party

15
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:26.613
'cause it sounds
(Patricia laughs)

16
00:00:26.613 --> 00:00:29.100
like actually like maybe something we could all adapt.

17
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:29.933
I don't know.
(Patricia laughs)

18
00:00:29.933 --> 00:00:31.180
It sounds so cool. What was it?

19
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:33.871
So when I turned 40, I had a wake for my youth.

20
00:00:33.871 --> 00:00:34.712
Yeah!

21
00:00:34.712 --> 00:00:36.050
So, yeah.
(audience applauds)

22
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.350
I had skull and crossbones.

23
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.870 line:15%
And people were making eulogies that were silly,

24
00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:43.450 line:15%
and tongue in cheek, and funny.

25
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.340 line:15%
And it was like, ah, let's bury that part of my life

26
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.270
and start anew.
(audience laughs)

27
00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.490
I've never heard of anyone doing that.

28
00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.270
And I feel like that is a trend

29
00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:53.930
that could pick up steam.
Yeah.

30
00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:55.117
Yeah, it was fun.
(audience applauds)

31
00:00:55.117 --> 00:00:56.543
It was really, really fun.

32
00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:58.680
Okay, well, I'm into that.

33
00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:02.169
And it is your birthday actually right now, right?

34
00:01:02.169 --> 00:01:04.980
(audience cheers)
(audience applauds)

35
00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.280
April 8th.

36
00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.923
Springtime, yup.

37
00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.910
I wish for all of your wishes to come true.

38
00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:14.390
Oh, thanks, honey.

39
00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:18.980
Okay, so okay, I usually have this like in my head,

40
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.880
but because I wasn't prepared...

41
00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.580
We were both rebellious teenagers.

42
00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:25.510
Yes, that's true.

43
00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:27.650
What's the craziest thing you ever did?

44
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:29.320
I can think of a lot.

45
00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.690
I mean, there are a lot.
(audience laughs)

46
00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.160
But crazy enough to talk about here?

47
00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:35.450
(audience laughs)

48
00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:37.950
Me and my friend got arrested shoplifting.

49
00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.170
And so I went to the police station,

50
00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.740
all that stuff, waited for them.

51
00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:46.450
And then when I had to go back, the judge,

52
00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.110
or I don't even know who this person was,

53
00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:50.910
mediator or something, anyway, whoever he was,

54
00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.590
he said, "Will you ever do this again?"

55
00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:53.423
And I said, "No."

56
00:01:53.423 --> 00:01:55.106
But he's like, "Okay, I believe you.

57
00:01:55.106 --> 00:01:57.320
I'm gonna let you off on a warning."

58
00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.470
And I said, "No, no, I think I should be punished.

59
00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.830
I don't think I should just be let off like that."

60
00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:06.790
And he was like, "Okay, okay. (laughs)

61
00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:08.140
How about this for punishment?

62
00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:10.640
You go to therapy until you think you're done."

63
00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:13.033
And I was like, "Okay, that sounds good.

64
00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:15.177
I'll go to therapy."

65
00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.240
Was the therapy good?

66
00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.290
Or was it like...

67
00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:19.540
Well, I love therapy,

68
00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.303
but I kept falling asleep in therapy.

69
00:02:21.303 --> 00:02:22.680
(audience laughs)

70
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:23.770
Fall asleep on the set.

71
00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.287
You fall asleep in therapy.
I know. (laughs)

72
00:02:25.287 --> 00:02:26.560
I'm kind of a sleeper.
I love that you're like,

73
00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.100
no, I would like the full extent-

74
00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.570
Of the punishment, yeah.

75
00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.610
Okay, you are obviously in "Severance,"

76
00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:35.677
